  "rules": {},
  "sections": {
    "bc314ab0": {
      "body": "Architecture mode, rebuilt from zero around one idea: the design is a drawing checked against the repo, like an as-built drawing in a real architect's office. Operate surface; variance 3, motion 2, density 6. The job: show what runs, and where the design and the repo disagree.\n\nPalette: drafting paper (#f6f7f5) with a cool green-grey temperature, ink for text and for the one primary action. Redline (#c0362c) has one job: a place where the repo and the design differ. Nothing else is red. Instrument Sans for the interface; JetBrains Mono only for things that are literally code: file paths, image tags, k8s names.\n\nThe bold thing: drift drawn on the map as redline markup, a struck value with the repo value written beside it, the way a checker marks up a drawing. A part only in the repo is drawn dashed in red; a part only in the design is struck through.\n\nNever: a monitoring dashboard (no live metrics, no health colours), the SaaS card kit, a blueprint-blue costume.",
      "heading": "Direction",
      "id": "bc314ab0",
      "index": "a0"
    }
  },
